# Internal-only (never committed)
.planning/
.serena/
.arcsop/

# Generated exports
output/

# Local demo sandboxes and generated chain state
/demo/
experiments/dynamic-midnight-sdk-validation/

# Build artefacts
/target/
**/target/
*.rlib
/midnight-level-db/
examples/passport-demo/.generated/
examples/passport-demo/public/zk/
# Both are staged by examples/passport-demo/scripts/prepare-zk-assets.mjs from
# the stagenet contract build. The compiled contract modules live inside the
# workspace so they resolve the ledger-9 compact-runtime; they are generated
# output either way and are never committed.
examples/passport-demo/contracts/stagenet/
# The stagenet contract build itself: ~103 MB of prover and verifier keys,
# produced by the deployment harness and shared with the demo through the
# staging script above. The rule lives in that directory's own .gitignore, which
# ignores managed/*/keys and managed/*/zkir and leaves the sources, the generated
# contract modules, and the manifests tracked.
#
# It used to be a blanket `examples/passport-balancer/contracts-stagenet/` here,
# which was a trap rather than a shortcut: git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so a NEW file anywhere under it — a renamed contract source, say —
# was invisible to `git status` and silently absent from the commit, while the
# files already tracked went on being tracked. It hid nothing the local rule and
# the `node_modules/` rule below do not already hide. Removed 2026/09/10.

# Vercel CLI link state and the locally assembled Build Output (see
# scripts/build-vercel-output.mjs). Never committed — the deployed artefacts
# are produced locally and uploaded with `vercel deploy --prebuilt`.
.vercel/

